From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert B. Calhoun <rcalhoun@shotspotter.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configure.ac, syscall.c: guard linux/openat2.h with HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H

rsync 3.4.0 introduced use of openat2() on Linux for secure relative path
opening (--open-nolinks). The header <linux/openat2.h> was added in kernel
5.6, but rsync includes it unconditionally for any Linux target, and
configure.ac never checks for its presence.

This breaks cross-compilation when the target's kernel headers are older
than 5.6 (e.g. kernel 4.x or 5.4 LTS targets).

Fix by:
 - Adding linux/openat2.h to the AC_CHECK_HEADERS probe in configure.ac,
   which sets HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H in config.h when the header is present.
 - Guarding the #include and the openat2() code paths in syscall.c with
   #ifdef HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H / #if defined(__linux__) && defined(HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H).

When the header is absent the openat2() code path is not compiled
and execution falls through to the existing portable per-component
O_NOFOLLOW fallback.

Signed-off-by: Robert B. Calhoun <rcalhoun@shotspotter.com>

---
 configure.ac | 2 +-
 syscall.c    | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/configure.ac	2026-06-03 05:01:01.411313350 +0000
+++ b/configure.ac	2026-06-03 05:01:06.471353680 +0000
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
     sys/un.h sys/attr.h arpa/inet.h arpa/nameser.h locale.h sys/types.h \
     netdb.h malloc.h float.h limits.h iconv.h libcharset.h langinfo.h mcheck.h \
     sys/acl.h acl/libacl.h attr/xattr.h sys/xattr.h sys/extattr.h dl.h \
-    popt.h popt/popt.h linux/falloc.h netinet/in_systm.h netgroup.h \
+    popt.h popt/popt.h linux/falloc.h linux/openat2.h netinet/in_systm.h netgroup.h \
     zlib.h xxhash.h openssl/md4.h openssl/md5.h zstd.h lz4.h sys/file.h \
     bsd/string.h)
 AC_CHECK_HEADERS([netinet/ip.h], [], [], [[#include <netinet/in.h>]])
--- a/syscall.c	2026-06-03 05:01:01.412313358 +0000
+++ b/syscall.c	2026-06-03 05:01:22.045477816 +0000
@@ -35,8 +35,10 @@
 
 #ifdef __linux__
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
+#ifdef HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H
 #include <linux/openat2.h>
 #endif
+#endif
 
 #include "ifuncs.h"
 
@@ -1691,7 +1693,7 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#ifdef __linux__
+#if defined(__linux__) && defined(HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H)
 static int secure_relative_open_linux(const char *basedir, const char *relpath, int flags, mode_t mode)
 {
 	struct open_how how;
@@ -1791,7 +1793,7 @@
 		return -1;
 	}
 
-#ifdef __linux__
+#if defined(__linux__) && defined(HAVE_LINUX_OPENAT2_H)
 	{
 		int fd = secure_relative_open_linux(basedir, relpath, flags, mode);
 		/* ENOSYS = kernel < 5.6 doesn't have the syscall even though
